{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-120688-r4524779","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Homemade Mixed Spice","sourcePageId":120688,"sourceRevision":"4524779","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-17T23:43:56Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Homemade%20Mixed%20Spice&oldid=4524779","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:25.425Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for spice mixes","Category:Recipes using allspice","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"0331c56e91aa047757cd5260545f21c25a4b5dd53fba40e230a18c91af5b0f97","sourceWikitext":"{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Spices and herbs|Spice]]\n{{recipesummary|category=Spice mix recipes|yield=¼ cup ({{convert|40|g|oz|abbr=on|disp=s}})||time=2 minutes|difficulty=1|image=[[Image:Mixed spices 01 Pengo.jpg|300px]]}}\n{{nutritionsummary|1 teaspoon (5 g)|8|7|0|0 g|0 g|0 mg|61 mg|1.7 g|0.1 g|1.2 g|0.1 g|0%|0%|0%|0%}}\n'''Mixed spice''', also '''pudding spice''', is a mix of sweet spices commonly used in [[Cookbook:Baking|baking]], [[Cookbook:Dessert|desserts]], and with [[Cookbook:Fruit|fruit]], particularly in [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United Kingdom|British cuisine]], and in cuisines that derive from it (e.g. the old colonies of the British empire). It is often sold premixed in grocery stores.\n\nThe mix almost always contains [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]], [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]], and [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]. Often, other spices are added to the mix, including [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]], [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]], [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]], caraway, [[Cookbook:Mace|mace]], and cayenne (historically).\n\n==Recipe==\nThis is a typical blend of spices used to make mixed spice.\n\n=== Ingredients ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] ground [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]]\n* 1 tablespoon ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 1 tablespoon ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] ground [[Cookbook:Mace|mace]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|Ginger]]\n\n=== Procedure ===\n\n# Blend all spices together, and store in a sealed jar away from light.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for spice mixes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using allspice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Homemade Mixed Spice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tablespoon ground allspice","sourceText":"1 tablespoon ground allspice","amountText":"1 tablespoon ground allspice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tablespoon ground cinnamon","sourceText":"1 tablespoon ground cinnamon","amountText":"1 tablespoon ground cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tablespoon ground nutmeg","sourceText":"1 tablespoon ground nutmeg","amountText":"1 tablespoon ground nutmeg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 teaspoons ground mace",